.TH proxytrack 1 "07 October 2026" "httrack website copier"
.SH NAME
proxytrack \- proxy to serve content archived by httrack website copier
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B proxytrack <proxy\-addr:proxy\-port> <ICP\-addr:ICP\-port> [archive ..] [\-\-list <file\-list>]
.br
.B proxytrack \-\-convert <output> [archive ..] [\-\-list <file\-list>]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B proxytrack
serves pages already archived by
.BR httrack (1)
without going online. It answers as an HTTP proxy on the first address, and to ICP queries from a parent proxy such as Squid on the second. It reads httrack caches
.RI ( hts\-cache/new.zip ,
or the older
.I new.ndx
with
.IR new.dat )
and
.I .arc
files. The archived content can also be browsed under
.I /webdav
on the proxy address.
.PP
With
.IR \-\-convert ,
it merges the archives into a single
.I .zip
cache or
.I .arc
file instead, then exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B archive
an httrack cache (new.zip, or new.ndx with new.dat) or an .arc file
.TP
.B \-\-list <file\-list>
read more archive paths from this file, one per line
.TP
.B \-\-convert <output>
merge the archives into one .zip or .arc file, then exit
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
print this help and exit
.TP
.B \-\-version
print the version and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B proxytrack localhost:8080 localhost:3130 /home/archives/example.com/hts\-cache/new.zip
serve that mirror as a proxy on port 8080, and answer ICP queries on port 3130
.TP
.B proxytrack \-\-convert /home/archives/merged.zip /home/archives/a/hts\-cache/new.zip /home/archives/b/hts\-cache/new.zip
merge two mirrors into merged.zip
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IP HTS_LOG
Set to a number above 0 to log more detail to the console.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Errors and warnings are written to the console.
